<title>UK: Capital Shopping Centres sets 204 mln stg convertible bond.</title>
<headline>Capital Shopping Centres sets 204 mln stg convertible bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Capital Shopping Centres Plc has issued a 204 million stg convertible bond issue, joint lead managers Merrill Lynch and UBS said.</p>
<p>The subordinated bond matures in December 2006, pays a 6.25 percent semi-annual coupon and is priced at par.  </p>
<p>The transaction has a seven-year hard no call. Conversion price is 3.70 pounds, a 9.47 percent premium over Monday's closing share price.</p>
<p>Listing is in London, denominations are 1,000 and governing law is English. Payment date is December 3.</p>
</text>
